},"end":{"line":102,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"PETSc has only one hard requirement which is the BLAS (Basic Linear Algebra Subprograms) library. BLAS is available on most systems but some packages provide optimized version of the libraries that are more efficient. In most cases we recommend using the OPENBLAS packages. The Intel Math Library (MKL) also provides optimized BLAS libraries, it is free and commonly available on HPC machines.","position":{"start":{"line":102,"column":1},"end":{"line":102,"column":1}},"key":"rrFUPODh5O"}],"key":"dmNdwToE16"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":104,"column":1},"end":{"line":104,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Like most external packages you can download OPENBLAS by passing the ","position":{"start":{"line":104,"column":1},"end":{"line":104,"column":1}},"key":"N6NOKQUVfz"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"--download-openblas","position":{"start":{"line":104,"column":1},"end":{"line":104,"column":1}},"key":"zF3ULDy0Xs"},{"type":"text","value":" command to the configuration script. At the time of writing this causes some errors and we chose to install OPENBLAS using the package manager of out LINUX distribution.","position":{"start":{"line":104,"column":1},"end":{"line":104,"column":1}},"key":"HIdbJMtZXl"}],"key":"LReaTRlMoe"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":106,"column":1},"end":{"line":106,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"strong","position":{"start":{"line":106,"column":1},"end":{"line":106,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Ubuntu","position":{"start":{"line":106,"column":1},"end":{"line":106,"column":1}},"key":"wrBEZKCctG"}],"key":"lNaNERhGaz"},{"type":"text","value":":","position":{"start":{"line":106,"column":1},"end":{"line":106,"column":1}},"key":"wgJWXH2I6K"}],"key":"UsRVorMw7F"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":108,"column":1},"end":{"line":108,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Note that Ubuntu provides a ","p